  "term": "endometrium",
  "definition": "The endometrium is the tissue lining of the uterus. In this source, it is described as a tissue that becomes receptive to conceptus signals during the peri-implantation period and includes glandular epithelial and stromal cells that can show molecular and inflammatory responses.",
